# The cgo crash walked backwards: the exported marker frame, the fault stack
# across the Go/C boundary, an instruction round trip through it, and the
# full register file (replay-only: the target description includes `Gs_base`,
# which is how Delve finds a goroutine's `g`).
break main.goMarker
continue
args
locals
stack 6
regs
step
bt 8
rev step-instruction
step-instruction
checkpoint c1
step
restart c1
stack 5
# The recorded fault: Delve reports the Windows exception code behind the
# SIGSEGV, which is what makes a TTD replay as informative as a live crash.
continue
stack 8
locals
exit
